# Redundancy Removal

This directory contains the steps used to identify and remove redundant CHIKV complete-genome sequences before downstream analysis.

Sequence redundancy was assessed using CD-HIT-EST at 100% sequence identity.

The resulting representative sequences were retained for subsequent genome-level analysis.

## Method

CD-HIT-EST was used with:

- Sequence identity threshold: 100%
- Alignment coverage requirement: 90%
- Global sequence identity: disabled
- Threads: 2

The CD-HIT cluster file was subsequently examined to identify representative and redundant sequences.

## Input

- Curated CHIKV complete-genome FASTA file

## Output

- CD-HIT representative FASTA file
- CD-HIT cluster file
- Redundancy verification report

No raw or unpublished sequence data are included in this repository.
